; StoreSessionDayOneCustomer — parked directly across the counter from the
; register, on the customer-facing service spot. Identity rotation = facing -Z
; (toward the counter); the player approaches from the front entrance
; and meets them face-to-face. The authored transform is the single
; source of truth (the controller does not override it at runtime).
; §F-PUNCH1 — Back-room enclosure. The back-room atmosphere props
; (RefurbBenchCrate, SortCartCrate, inventory shelf, damaged bin) live
; under the `back_room` Node3D, which is added to STORE_SESSION_KEEP_ROOT_NODES
; so they're visible during store_session. These walls form a south + west
; partition with a 1.5 m doorway gap centered on the south face, so the
; player approaches from the storefront side and walks in.
[node name="StoreSessionBackroomWallSide" type="Node3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 4.05, 1.75, -8.375)

[node name="WallMesh" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="StoreSessionBackroomWallSide"]
